Lets say the elastic is set up along with some DB - we need to sync the changes.

To make sure the data in Elasticsearch is always in sync with the data in our SQL DB,
we can use change data capture (CDC) for real-time or near-real-time data synchronization 
from PostgreSQL to Elasticsearch. 

This setup captures changes in the PostgreSQL database, such as inserts, updates, and deletes, and replicates them to the Elasticsearch index.



CDC = Change Data Capture

CDC is a mechanism to detect changes happening in a database and capture those changes as events.


Suppose you have:

PostgreSQL
    |
    | INSERT / UPDATE / DELETE
    ↓
   CDC
    |
    ↓
Change Events
    |
    ↓
Kafka
    |
    ├──> Elasticsearch
    ├──> Data Warehouse
    └──> Analytics



Example

Suppose your product is stored in PostgreSQL:

Product
id = 101
name = "Nike Shoes"
price = 5000

Someone changes the price:

UPDATE products
SET price = 4500
WHERE id = 101;

CDC captures this change:

{
  "operation": "UPDATE",
  "productId": 101,
  "oldPrice": 5000,
  "newPrice": 4500
}

That event can be published to Kafka:

Postgres
    |
    | Price updated
    ↓
CDC Tool
(Debezium)
    |
    ↓
Kafka
    |
    ↓
Elasticsearch
    |
    ↓
Search now shows ₹4500





How does CDC know about changes?

The common approach is log-based CDC.

For example, PostgreSQL maintains a Write-Ahead Log (WAL).

Application
     |
     | UPDATE
     ↓
PostgreSQL
     |
     ├── Update Database
     |
     └── Write to WAL
             |
             ↓
       CDC Connector
             |
             ↓
           Kafka

A CDC tool like Debezium reads the database's transaction log/WAL and converts changes into events.





Why use CDC?
1. Keep Elasticsearch synchronized
Postgres (Source of Truth)
        |
        ↓
       CDC
        |
        ↓
      Kafka
        |
        ↓
 Elasticsearch

Instead of your application doing:

Update Postgres
Update Elasticsearch

you only update Postgres:

Update Postgres
      ↓
CDC captures change
      ↓
Kafka
      ↓
Elasticsearch updated

This reduces coupling.





2. Analytics
Postgres
    ↓
   CDC
    ↓
  Kafka
    ├──> Data Warehouse
    ├──> ClickHouse
    └──> Analytics

You can stream database changes into analytical systems.






CDC vs Event-Driven Architecture

They are related but not the same.

Event-driven architecture
Your application explicitly publishes a business event:

Order Service
     |
     | publish OrderCreated
     ↓
   Kafka
     |
    CDC

The database change is captured automatically:

Order Service
     |
     | INSERT
     ↓
Postgres
     |
     ↓
    CDC
     |
     ↓
Kafka
Interview distinction

CDC captures changes from a database and publishes them as events. 
Event-driven architecture is the broader architectural pattern where services communicate through events. 
CDC can be one mechanism used to implement event-driven systems.

